<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Hardened-runtime entitlements — kept to the MINIMUM a bundled-CPython
    (PyInstaller) app actually needs, and no more.

    cs.disable-library-validation — REQUIRED. The bundle ships C-extension
    dylibs from pip wheels (numpy, scipy, lxml, pydantic_core, Pillow) that
    are signed by THEIR authors, not this app's Team ID. Without this the
    hardened runtime refuses to load them and the app will not launch.

    Removed (were set true historically — cargo-culted to brute-force past
    earlier notarization errors, NOT because anything requires them):
      • cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory — W^X / JIT memory. CPython +
        numpy/scipy never request it. Safe to drop.
      • cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables — modern PyInstaller resolves
        bundled libs via @rpath/@loader_path, not DYLD_* env vars.

    GATE: the v2.0.3 macOS DMG must be LAUNCH-tested (actually open the
    notarized .app), not just VERSION-checked, before shipping. If it fails
    to open, re-add allow-dyld-environment-variables first (the likelier of
    the two), re-notarize, re-launch — never re-add blindly.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
